{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB05013 - MONDO_8420",
  "verbalization": "Ingenol Mebutate is implicated in the pathogenesis of Seborrheic Keratosis through a chain of indications that ultimately link it to this condition. The evidence suggests that Ingenol Mebutate, through its indication for Keratoacanthoma and Actinic Cheilitis, activates a metabolic pathway involving Aminolevulinic Acid, which is also linked to Seborrheic Keratosis. This indicates a potential role in the development of Seborrheic Keratosis via a shared biochemical mechanism involving Aminolevulinic Acid. The presence of multiple indirect pathways, all leading through Aminolevulinic Acid to Seborrheic Keratosis, suggests a possible convergent pathway or a shared intermediate in the development of the condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Aminolevulinic Acid in the context of Seborrheic Keratosis, though the exact mechanism by which Ingenol Mebutate influences this pathway remains to be fully elucidated.",
